.TH CRYPTOMAKO 1 "September 2026" "cryptomako" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cryptomako \- Cryptomator format-8 vault CLI (S3 / local) for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cryptomako
[\fIglobal flags\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CryptoMako unlocks Cryptomator
.B format 8
(SIV_GCM) vaults over HTTPS SigV4 (path-style) or a local vault directory.
Cleartext UX locally; ciphertext stays in the object store. Remote put/delete fail closed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B unlock
Unlock and print vault metadata.
.TP
.B ls
List cleartext paths (optional
.BR --recursive ).
.TP
.B cat
Print a cleartext file.
.TP
.B mount
FUSE cleartext mount (default read-only;
.B --rw
for writable fail-closed puts/deletes).
.TP
.B sync
Encrypt a local tree into the vault (honors Backup Sync excludes).
.TP
.B fixture
Create a minimal format-8 vault for smoke tests.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.BR --local " PATH"
Unlock a vault directory on disk.
.TP
.BR --endpoint " URL"
S3 API URL (HTTPS, no bucket in path).
.TP
.BR --bucket " NAME"
Bucket name.
.TP
.BR --prefix " PREFIX"
Vault prefix inside the bucket.
.TP
.BR --access-key " ID"
Access key id (non-secret).
.TP
.BR --config " PATH"
JSON config (default
.IR ~/.config/cryptomako/config.json ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRYPTOMAKO_PASSWORD
Vault passphrase (required). Never put in JSON or argv.
.TP
.B CRYPTOMAKO_SECRET_KEY
S3 secret access key (remote only). Never put in JSON.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cryptomako/config.json
Non-secret connection settings (
.BR endpoint ,
.BR region ,
.BR bucket ,
.BR prefix ,
.BR accessKey ,
.BR pathStyle ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/cryptomako/backup-sync-excludes.json
Backup Sync excludes (
.BR directoryNames ,
.BR fileNames ,
.BR fileExtensions ), macOS-compatible.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full docs in
.I /usr/share/doc/cryptomako/README.md
and the upstream linux/README.md.
